ity"},{"text":"Forest rights/community interactions"},{"text":"Environmental protection"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact legal provisions, departmental powers and recruitment requirements should be studied from the current applicable central and state rules."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Forest Guard, practical knowledge of the relevant state Forest Department procedures is particularly important."}]},{"heading":"Community & Conservation Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Forest conservation often involves interaction with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Local communities"},{"text":"Farmers"},{"text":"Tribal communities"},{"text":"Forest-dependent households"},{"text":"Researchers"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Forest officers"},{"text":"Wildlife organizations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Community engagement"},{"text":"Conflict de-escalation"},{"text":"Conservation awareness"},{"text":"Field reporting"},{"text":"Teamwork"}]}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Local Biodiversity Survey"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a structured survey of a local ecosystem."},{"type":"p","text":"Record:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Species"},{"text":"Habitat"},{"text":"Abundance"},{"text":"GPS location"},{"text":"Signs"},{"text":"Threats"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Species database"},{"text":"Biodiversity summary"},{"text":"GIS map"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Forest Fire Risk Mapping"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a GIS-based forest-fire risk map using:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vegetation"},{"text":"Land cover"},{"text":"Elevation"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Historical fire data"},{"text":"Distance from roads/settlements"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["QGIS","satellite data","Python."],"sep":"+","label":"Tools"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Camera-Trap Wildlife Analysis"},{"type":"p",